HOTFIX 2: after a successful install the machine now REBOOTS instead of
          falling back into the installer menu.  ISO GRUB detects the
          installed system and makes it the default (T14); UEFI also
          gets a real NVRAM BootNext entry (T16).  Remove the USB stick when
          prompted so the firmware cannot boot the installer again.

HOTFIX  : default GRUB entries use console=tty0 ONLY.  The old
          'console=tty0 console=ttyS0,115200' bound /dev/console to the
          LAST console (the COM port), so on a PC without a serial port
          the installer UI was invisible: one blinking cursor, top left.
          T12 proves the installer runs and writes the disk with VGA only;
          T13 proves the GRUB menu and the installer dialog are ACTUALLY
          drawn on the VGA framebuffer (raw QMP screendumps, lit-pixel
          counts ~28,700 / 261,379).  Safe text mode entry added as fallback.

